Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] document the seccomp backend; probe harness teardown fix;
 live evidence

* --backend documented in the man page and --help; --backend wired into
  the option-wiring experiment.
* experiments/15-senotif-primitives.sh: the six ptrace-free primitives
  proven on the ptrace-denied development host (logs committed); the
  probe harness fixes its own teardown race (break on exit_group,
  bounded poll-reap).
* experiments/50-live-comparison.sh now runs live on this host via the
  auto backend (timeout-guarded, vanilla baseline skipped with notice
  where ptrace is denied): LD_DEBUG=libs 0 hits / 0 lines where the
  report records the dlopen probes and static-binary paths.
* validate.sh: T1 environmental guard (if TRACEME fails even untraced,
  the spoof is not assertable on that host), T2/T3/T4/T5 preconditions
  fixed for the seccomp world, T6 judged by its report (the preset's
  keep-alive budget legitimately ends in a mirrored SIGSEGV).
* README/NEWS: the 'cannot run here' caveat is gone -- the matrix runs
  live on the ptrace-denied development host.
* docs/reviews/REVIEW-4: the pass that reviewed running code, with the
  twelve findings it produced (mm-pinning, entry-phase state, qual
  flags, line bookkeeping, ret:null semantics, report quoting, loop
  hang, exit-code teardown race, and the rest).
